{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_117d5b932ab2dc04cb2b29d749481e018a2b03714517bba6b9bdab72d3da06e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"web_fetch is SSRF-guarded, refusing RFC1918, loopback, and cloud-metadata targets unless BANDIT_ALLOW_PRIVATE_WEB_FETCH=1 is set."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1dbbbdb85218b30d9152e205e6bc411774314fa1eb5e154ddf2245e36d97dc0b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Stated design rules include local models as first-class citizens, one host-agnostic runtime, language adapters validating before write so invalid content never reaches disk, and intent-based skill activation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3570b701bdb26bed063ca22ce75d9f3e28d8ef66bf4ba9fca0a6dcc7220a78f3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent auto-loads BANDIT.md, CLAUDE.md, or AGENTS.md from the workspace root into the system prompt; /remember appends facts and /init scaffolds a new BANDIT.md."},{"claim_ids":["clm_368c811b2f240b0eb27d8d650b71cbf0e30518db9771dcd1e0cf829ceca18eeb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prompts can prefix a path with @ to inline file contents before the model sees them, up to 8 mentions per prompt at 64 KB each with auto-truncation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_684a550a16caee7f470af13ddda067f9f4da2aa8d1f58bc88d8b6581bd1dc23e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The default skill set includes always-on filesystem and git skills plus context-triggered code review, testing, planning, semantic search, and Gmail-dependent mail search skills."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e0a4441f147aec848bce9c9bb65b312e48ffc98c4eae25fd36a05842ffff777"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run pnpm test (what CI runs on PRs), add contract tests for new behaviors, and add real-trace replay fixtures for recurring failure modes per the agent-core test docs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e716087bf8447d90a47a8bc062defccc9343339f0d2ea65157bf89072c3aa0e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Auto mode runs routine work unprompted but always asks before destructive actions (deletions, history rewrites, credential files, exfiltration-style sends), and this floor cannot be disabled by settings or saved allow rules."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7f949bfb1e8a5de4019db59c9021065ca79d964b271e0aab8f2194fafcdd3b5b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"REPL sessions persist as JSONL under ~/.bandit/sessions/ and can be resumed via bandit --resume or /session resume."},{"claim_ids":["clm_80552685c338060e46d875c12c80b31b61e7337a6c99684fd454ece4f28d0233"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent can spawn background subagents whose synopses inject into the parent's next iteration; /tasks inspects and cancels them, and stopping cascades to in-flight subagents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86c2c1a06c2562134d3d737bf93c7378657c9c112f083261cd1f2a844d8683fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README lists maturing areas: plan mode in the CLI, status-line/TUI polish, and lossless trace replay for native-tool runs; PreToolUse hook failures warn but do not yet abort."},{"claim_ids":["clm_98d0a292e320cc708dde134f1e1cbf94eccf13812eb6a40e66ad61c5e0e469b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships two hosts — a VS Code/Cursor extension (Bandit Stealth) and a terminal CLI — both backed by the same stealth-core-runtime package, with skills, memory files, and hooks working identically across them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a038da8ae22405f36d982eb495b5528892dcfae8b635cfcff48c01474f92bfe5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A MEMORY.md topic index (capped at 4 KB) loads every turn while linked memory/ files (32 KB cap) are lazily fetched via read_memory when the task matches."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a2287ad834121f12a6c0d5acc61f674360815699748900a7c9f4390a7900e309"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Bandit speaks MCP as both client and server: MCP server tools surface as <server>.<tool>, and 'bandit mcp serve' exposes native tools over stdio with a --read-only mode."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a9d3ebab90df761807b0c54ea64938edde31f9c4a7acb025d701b97ed849f3fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills are markdown files with YAML frontmatter in .bandit/skills/ that load on the next turn; triggers are regex matches on the user prompt, activation:always skills run every turn, and legacy JSON skills still load."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ac5ff94bc857614f3616ae21e74660dff389c3014232521bd2d7bff1d4e5bc2e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The runtime targets Ollama (local daemon or Ollama Cloud via the same API) and optionally Bandit Cloud hosted inference; web_search uses Tavily with a TAVILY_API_KEY."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b3b7e55327a9f0b522b19994c79eaa233f03d7dff3fc50dd039d3b2effac0bce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool-use loop is capped by BANDIT_MAX_ITERATIONS (default 20); a documented benchmark run hit this ceiling and was forced to synthesize after 13 exploration rounds."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b4cf88bb45a9446372f3045c3c8b769337cc985b5912824d46df790098820d3b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers slash commands including /help, /doctor, /model, /skills, /session, /memory, /remember, /trace, /insights, and /exit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5bf5513b4c9e4e4eabf5963d91d9c1128296926518a6a8754c0e250fc52d6fd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every file-edit tool call passes an approval gate that shows a compact diff before touching disk, with scoped grant options such as allow once, allow turn, allow session, always allow, and deny; approving a command grants only that command pattern."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e0cc24667cc91c70001515cff6d6e5b39e178622f92fee0ca28f9ce1a9e39100"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README reports two reproducible benchmark runs of the agent on repo deep-dive prompts, with metrics like turn duration, LLM iterations, and tool-call counts, plus reproduction commands."}],"claim_ids":["clm_117d5b932ab2dc04cb2b29d749481e018a2b03714517bba6b9bdab72d3da06e4","clm_1dbbbdb85218b30d9152e205e6bc411774314fa1eb5e154ddf2245e36d97dc0b","clm_3570b701bdb26bed063ca22ce75d9f3e28d8ef66bf4ba9fca0a6dcc7220a78f3","clm_368c811b2f240b0eb27d8d650b71cbf0e30518db9771dcd1e0cf829ceca18eeb","clm_684a550a16caee7f470af13ddda067f9f4da2aa8d1f58bc88d8b6581bd1dc23e","clm_7e0a4441f147aec848bce9c9bb65b312e48ffc98c4eae25fd36a05842ffff777","clm_7e716087bf8447d90a47a8bc062defccc9343339f0d2ea65157bf89072c3aa0e","clm_7f949bfb1e8a5de4019db59c9021065ca79d964b271e0aab8f2194fafcdd3b5b","clm_80552685c338060e46d875c12c80b31b61e7337a6c99684fd454ece4f28d0233","clm_86c2c1a06c2562134d3d737bf93c7378657c9c112f083261cd1f2a844d8683fb","clm_98d0a292e320cc708dde134f1e1cbf94eccf13812eb6a40e66ad61c5e0e469b9","clm_a038da8ae22405f36d982eb495b5528892dcfae8b635cfcff48c01474f92bfe5","clm_a2287ad834121f12a6c0d5acc61f674360815699748900a7c9f4390a7900e309","clm_a9d3ebab90df761807b0c54ea64938edde31f9c4a7acb025d701b97ed849f3fb","clm_ac5ff94bc857614f3616ae21e74660dff389c3014232521bd2d7bff1d4e5bc2e","clm_b3b7e55327a9f0b522b19994c79eaa233f03d7dff3fc50dd039d3b2effac0bce","clm_b4cf88bb45a9446372f3045c3c8b769337cc985b5912824d46df790098820d3b","clm_d5bf5513b4c9e4e4eabf5963d91d9c1128296926518a6a8754c0e250fc52d6fd","clm_e0cc24667cc91c70001515cff6d6e5b39e178622f92fee0ca28f9ce1a9e39100"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_821a31576a1041afbf3af89db5739308","id":"pg_00477ce93dd85f4d8478ba0e12cc7a38","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/burtson-labs-bandit-agent-framework-readme-md-e926d20a48e6-ba0e12cc7a38.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_79d1725cc298549eb0d057a2427ab10d"],"title":"Burtson-Labs/bandit-agent-framework/README.md @ e926d20a48e6","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_821a31576a1041afbf3af89db5739308"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_ee038efea301253a57025e31e3e1732a13a67723e006b543c821114418a3408f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the repo's own BANDIT.md instructs agents to read files before editing, prefer replace_range for large changes, run typecheck/smoke/vitest before claiming done, and bump versions without amending tagged releases."}],"claim_ids":["clm_ee038efea301253a57025e31e3e1732a13a67723e006b543c821114418a3408f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_821a31576a1041afbf3af89db5739308","id":"pg_3251b2bc0975585ba3a917f875091642","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/burtson-labs-bandit-agent-framework-bandit-md-e926d20a48e6-17f875091642.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_bc7753e9b8c354f980e9e29b6e86d784"],"title":"Burtson-Labs/bandit-agent-framework/BANDIT.md @ e926d20a48e6","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:38:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_821a31576a1041afbf3af89db5739308"}
